133389	133398	133399	133399	Svidrigaïlov	129	“ No ? You do n’t think so ? ”
133408	133572	133399	133399	Svidrigaïlov	129	“ But what do you say to this argument ( help me with it ): ghosts are , as it were , shreds and fragments of other worlds , the beginning of them . A man in health has , of course , no reason to see them , because he is above all a man of this earth and is bound for the sake of completeness and order to live only in this life . But as soon as one is ill , as soon as the normal earthly order of the organism is broken , one begins to realise the possibility of another world ; and the more seriously ill one is , the closer becomes one ’s contact with that other world , so that as soon as the man dies he steps straight into that world . I thought of that long ago . If you believe in a future life , you could believe in that , too . ”
133573	133583	133585	133585	Raskolnikov	102	“ I do n’t believe in a future life , ”
