133624	133691	133622	133622	Raskolnikov	102	“ We always imagine eternity as something beyond our conception , something vast , vast ! But why must it be vast ? Instead of all that , what if it ’s one little room , like a bath house in the country , black and grimy and spiders in every corner , and that ’s all eternity is ? I sometimes fancy it like that . ”
